{
  // Cloudflare's dashboard now provisions new projects as a Worker (via
  // "Create app" + a GitHub connection, deploying with `wrangler deploy`),
  // not the older, separately-branded "Pages" product — see the git history
  // around 2026-09-02 for why this file exists instead of Pages' zero-config
  // functions/ directory. `assets.directory` serves the Vite build output;
  // any request that doesn't match a static file (i.e. /api/*) falls
  // through to the Worker script at `main`.
  "name": "habit-assistant",
  "main": "src/server/worker.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-17",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist"
  },
  // Non-secret runtime vars belong here, not only in the dashboard: a
  // dashboard-only "Text" variable does NOT carry forward into a new
  // version built by a Git-triggered `wrangler deploy` (learned 2026-09-03
  // the hard way — TRIAL_PROVIDER silently reverted to the code's "gemini"
  // fallback on the very next push, sending a Gemini key to Groq's API).
  // Secrets (TRIAL_API_KEY, TRIAL_FALLBACK_API_KEY, STT_TRIAL_API_KEY) stay
  // dashboard/CI-managed only — never put real key values in this file.
  //
  // TRIAL_FALLBACK_PROVIDER/TRIAL_FALLBACK_API_KEY: §23's automatic
  // cross-provider failover (handleAgentRequest.ts) supports a second
  // trial provider, but deliberately NOT enabled here yet. Verified
  // 2026-09-04: every current Groq model with tool-calling support (its
  // only realistic candidate) hard-rejects this app's full tool-schema
  // payload on its free tier (7,000-8,000 TPM/ITPM vs. an ~8,670-10,550
  // token request) — see groq.ts's defaultModel comment. Enabling Groq as
  // the fallback today would add a network round-trip that fails the same
  // way every time on a real Gemini outage, not add real resilience. Wire
  // this up once §24 shrinks the payload (or a better secondary appears).
  "vars": {
    "TRIAL_PROVIDER": "gemini"
  },
  // Enabled 2026-09-03 while debugging the Gemini tool-schema rejection —
  // without this, provider error bodies (logged via console.error in
  // handleAgentRequest.ts) go nowhere. Keeping it on: it's what let us find
  // the newCategoryId enum bug, and free tier covers 200K events/day.
  "observability": {
    "logs": {
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
